>She tried to _______ out the sauce with a little water, but it still tasted too rich. <em>(h\u00edg\u00edt \/ felh\u00edg\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p>The argument was based on a _______ premise, making the whole conclusion unreliable. <em>(gyenge \/ alaptalan)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">sov\u00e1ny \/ v\u00e9kony \/ h\u00edg<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): k\u00f6v\u00e9r \/ vastag \/ s\u0171r\u0171<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ layer = egy v\u00e9kony r\u00e9teg (pl. A thin layer of ice covered the pond.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ air = ritka leveg\u0151 (pl. Mountaineers often struggle with the thin air at high altitudes.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 wear _______ = elkopik, elv\u00e9konyodik (pl. The carpet was starting to wear thin in places.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ on top = ritkul\u00f3 haj\u00fa (pl. He was getting a bit thin on top.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ out = felh\u00edg\u00edt, elv\u00e9kony\u00edt (pl. You can thin out the paint with a little water.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>thin<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>thin<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>thinly<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>thinness<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>thin<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: thin crust \/ thin line \/ thin ice \/ thin air<\/span><\/p><p>similar: slender \/ skinny \/ lean \/ sparse<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: thick \/ fat \/ dense<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"new","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":null,"reviewed_on":null,"due_at":null,"previous_state":null},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"4 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-0